  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive verb ({自動詞|じどうし}). Related transitive form: {揉|も}む (to massage; to rub).\n\nUSAGE:\n{揉|も}める specifically refers to interpersonal or inter-party conflicts and disputes. Common contexts include:\n- お{金|かね}で{揉|も}める - to fight over money\n- {遺産|いさん}で{揉|も}める - to dispute over inheritance\n- {離婚|りこん}で{揉|も}める - to have conflicts during divorce\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜と{揉|も}める (to have a dispute with ~)\n- 〜のことで{揉|も}める (to fight over ~)\n- {揉|も}め{事|ごと} (trouble, dispute - noun form)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {揉|も}め{事|ごと} - trouble, dispute\n- {揉|も}め{合|あ}う - to struggle/scuffle together\n\nREGISTER:\nCasual to neutral. Common in everyday conversation.",
